le listen to radio won't  even know that the images are going by  but people who watch television see the  film and photos of the independent  journalists who are out there  videographers and photographers and also  corporate those who work for the network  so don't get some of this stuff on their  stations it's very important I'm not for  reality television except when it comes  to war then I am for showing exactly  what's happening when it comes to money  on this book are you taking the money  yourself  no the royalties are for Democracy Now  which is a non-profit why don't you take  it yourself because I want to shore up  independent media in fact we're on a  more than seventy City book and media  tour called the exception to the rulers  tour and we are going from independent  radio station to IND  pennant radio station we start in Bai  big fundraiser for WBA I headed on the  55th anniversary of Pacifica KPFA to a  big celebration there and made our way  to Los Angeles and each of these hit Los  Angeles 2,000 people came out in  Minneapolis kay FAI the big community  radio station there we did a big  fundraiser 1500 people came out and I  think it is about a tremendous hunger  for independent voices people hungry for  searching for not the views of a fringe  minority as I was saying I mean I've  come to think about the corporate  networks in this way you have all of  these pundits actually it's a very small  group of them who know so little about  so much I'm beginning to think they sit  in a room and they just changed the logo  throughout the day CBS NBC ABC now  they're wringing their hands how did we  get it so wrong about weapons of mass  destruction why not invite someone into  the studios who got it right and who got  it right more than a year ago when it  mattered who is questioning the  credibility of the so called  intelligence and I'm not talking about  just people outside the system outside  the establishment but people in the  establishment people in 